/*
  PDFRender - Photoshop PSD decoding.

  A PSD is a stack of layers, but every file ends with a flattened
  composite of the whole image - which is what Photoshop puts there so
  that other software can show the picture without understanding
  layers, and is exactly what a previewer wants.  That composite is
  what this reads.

  Greyscale, RGB, indexed and CMYK, 8 or 16 bits a channel, raw or
  PackBits.  Layers, masks, adjustment layers and colour profiles are
  all ignored: the composite already has them applied.

